Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Notify the ARM64EC emulator of direct image mappings

Applications such as CLR map SEC_IMAGE sections without calling LdrLoadDll.
ArbitraryUserPointer is a loader detail, not a property of an executable image.
Skipping these mappings leaves FEX unaware of executable image sections and
causes an execute access violation despite PAGE_EXECUTE_READ protection.

Retain the SectionImageInformation check so ordinary data mappings are not
sent to the image callback.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -733,7 +733,6 @@ static void notify_map_view_of_section( HANDLE handle, void *addr, SIZE_T size, ULONG alloc,
     NTSTATUS status;
 
     if (!pNotifyMapViewOfSection) return;
-    if (!NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.ArbitraryUserPointer) return;
     if (NtQuerySection( handle, SectionImageInformation, &info, sizeof(info), NULL )) return;
     status = pNotifyMapViewOfSection( NULL, addr, NULL, size, alloc, protect );
     if (NT_SUCCESS(status)) return;
